  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Breaking the Link: Ending Deforestation in Commodity Supply Chains</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Thematic area: Sustainable commodity production
Problem to be solved: Unsustainable land use and pressure on forests from global markets/leading companies.
Proposed solution (Impact &#x2013; outcomes - outputs) and target group: The project will reduce tropical deforestation by driving change through agricultural commodity supply chains. It will focus on soy
and cattle in Colombia.

The project will benefit local and Indigenous people; Enhancing recognition of Indigenous rights and territories and protecting forests that support livelihoods. 

The project aims to help achieve sustainable land use and reduce pressure on forests from global markets, and cuts across NICFI priorities.
Outcome: Reducing cattle and soy-driven deforestation by 85% in Colombia.

Partner: Fundacion EnvolVert</narrative>
  </description>
